    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0025" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg21"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">762.94/319: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-04-19T16:00:00+09:00">April 19, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 19—3:46 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>186. During the last few days I have received informal and personal assurances
                    from several well informed Japanese, of unimpeachable reliability, that I need
                    no longer worry over the possibility of Japan entering into a general alliance
                    with Germany and Italy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
